{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2442","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2442","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2442\",\"parent_revision\":\"c127d14d1a89c3f1c82e451b1f6afee8ff50f968d64984473a4d3870561b4dc8\",\"root_revision\":\"c127d14d1a89c3f1c82e451b1f6afee8ff50f968d64984473a4d3870561b4dc8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-08\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nLocalFilesystemArtifactProvider uses integer 0 as a sentinel value when issue_number is a beads string ID (e.g. bd-a3f8), because ArtifactManifest.issue_number is typed as int. This means filesystem artifact manifests stored for beads-backed issues incorrectly record issue_number as 0 rather than the actual beads ID. If multiple beads-backed issues store artifacts to the same local filesystem provider, their manifests all record issue_number=0, making cross-issue lookup unreliable. The issue_number field on ArtifactManifest needs to be widened to str | int, and the sentinel pattern replaced with proper beads ID storage.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **localfilesystemartifactprovider uses 0 as sentinel for beads string issue ids** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG T1 code review advisory item C \u2014 commit 8a37fd14, session 2026-05-15\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\nAll required inputs are AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE from direct codebase inspection.\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Bug description is precise: `ArtifactManifest(issue_number=0)` in `_fetch_issue_and_manifest` \u2014 sentinel int in place of actual beads string ID |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Fix is localized to `beads_artifact_provider.py:_fetch_issue_and_manifest` (2 call sites: lines 577, 579). `ArtifactManifest.issue_number` already typed `str | int` \u2014 no model change needed |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `ArtifactManifest` Pydantic model (`models.py:1386`) already accepts `str | int`. `BeadsArtifactProvider` has `issue_id: str` at all call sites |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | NEVER cast over Pydantic model; NEVER use `object` or `Any`; widen to `str | int` (already done at model level) \u2014 fix must thread `issue_id` through to `ArtifactManifest` constructor |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `_fetch_issue_and_manifest(issue_id: str)` already receives the beads ID string; the two `ArtifactManifest(issue_number=0)` constructors simply discard it |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Tests exist in `test_artifact_provider_item_id_coercion.py`; new unit tests must assert `get_manifest_bd(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` returns `manifest.issue_number == \\\"bd-a3f8\\\"` |\\n\\n**Issue Classification:** `defect` \u2014 incorrect value stored at a specific code location with a clear correct fix.\\n\\n**Design Intent Alignment:** `ArtifactManifest.issue_number` was explicitly widened to `str | int` (models.py line 1386 docstring: \\\"str UUID for Linear, str nanoid for beads\\\") to accommodate non-integer backends. The sentinel `0` pattern contradicts that intent by discarding the actual beads ID.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Enable the beads backend: `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads`\\n2. Call `artifact_list(issue_number=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` or `get_manifest_bd(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` on a beads-backed issue\\n3. Inspect the returned `ArtifactManifest` \u2014 observe `issue_number == 0` instead of `\\\"bd-a3f8\\\"`\\n4. With two distinct beads issues (e.g. `bd-a3f8` and `bd-b1c2`), both return `issue_number=0` \u2014 manifests are ambiguous (cannot distinguish which issue a cached/serialized manifest belongs to)\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Source: `backends/beads_artifact_provider.py` lines 577 and 579 \u2014 `return ArtifactManifest(issue_number=0), issue` \u2014 integer 0 hardcoded instead of `issue_id`\\n- Docstring at line 385 acknowledges the problem: \\\"issue_number is 0 for manifests returned from the beads backend\\\" \u2014 the bug is self-documented\\n- `models.py:1386` already typed `str | int` \u2014 model is correct; the provider discards the actual ID\\n- `LocalFilesystemArtifactProvider` does NOT have this bug: line 113 passes `item_id` directly\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 The beads backend is an opt-in deployment (requires `.beads/dh-backend` marker). Cross-issue manifest confusion only materialises when multiple beads-backed issues are active simultaneously. No data is lost \u2014 manifests are stored correctly in bd metadata; the issue_number field on the in-memory model is wrong. Surfaced in code review advisory (commit 8a37fd14), not a live incident.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Affects: BeadsArtifactProvider only. LocalFilesystemArtifactProvider correctly passes item_id through.\\n- Any consumer using manifest.issue_number for cache keying, display, or cross-reference sees 0 instead of the actual beads ID.\\n- Related defect: #2438 (str-first union ordering in MCP tool params) is a companion P1 bug affecting integer GitHub IDs \u2014 independent and can be fixed separately.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Manifests for beads-backed issues carry their actual ID, enabling correct cache keying, audit logging, and cross-issue comparisons\\n- Eliminates silent ambiguity where `issue_number=0` could match any cached manifest\\n- Aligns BeadsArtifactProvider with the design intent of `ArtifactManifest.issue_number: str | int`\\n- Removes an explicitly documented workaround from the codebase (the docstring that says \\\"0 because no integer ID applies\\\" can be replaced with accurate documentation)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `BeadsArtifactProvider.get_manifest_bd(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` is called, the returned `ArtifactManifest.issue_number` equals `\\\"bd-a3f8\\\"`. When the manifest is empty (no artifacts stored), `issue_number` is still `\\\"bd-a3f8\\\"`, not `0`. The same holds for any beads ID string.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `_fetch_issue_and_manifest(issue_id: str)` passes `issue_id` to the `ArtifactManifest(issue_number=issue_id)` constructor in both empty-manifest return paths (lines 577 and 579)\\n- No change to `ArtifactManifest` model (already `str | int`)\\n- No change to `LocalFilesystemArtifactProvider` (already correct)\\n- Docstring at line 385 updated to reflect actual behavior\\n- Two new unit tests in `tests/test_artifact_provider_item_id_coercion.py` or a new test file covering the beads provider: one for empty-manifest path, one for no-metadata path\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `BeadsArtifactProvider.get_manifest_bd(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` returns an `ArtifactManifest` where `manifest.issue_number == \\\"bd-a3f8\\\"` when `bd show` returns no metadata\\n2. `BeadsArtifactProvider.get_manifest_bd(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` returns an `ArtifactManifest` where `manifest.issue_number == \\\"bd-a3f8\\\"` when `bd show` returns metadata containing no `dh.artifacts` key\\n3. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -x` passes with no regressions\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_artifact_provider.py` exits 0\\n5. `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_artifact_provider.py` exits 0 (no new type errors)\\n6. The string literal `issue_number=0` no longer appears in `beads_artifact_provider.py`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_artifact_provider.py` (lines 577, 579 \u2014 the two sentinel sites) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` (line 1386 \u2014 `ArtifactManifest.issue_number: str \\\\| int`) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider_local.py` (lines 111-118 \u2014 correct reference implementation) |\\n| Prior test | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_artifact_provider_item_id_coercion.py` \u2014 pattern for provider ID tests |\\n| Agent | `@dh:backlog-item-groomer` |\\n| Related bug | #2438 \u2014 companion defect (str-first union ordering in MCP tool params) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `ArtifactManifest.issue_number` is already `str | int`; model change is complete\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. Root cause, affected lines, and correct fix are all directly observable.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 2-line change in `beads_artifact_provider.py` (pass `issue_id` instead of `0` in both empty-manifest return paths), docstring update, and 2 new unit tests. No model changes required.\\n\",\"digest\":\"d1f2f6edfca5957893c039f80779e59a4a4d9bff887d901073ebb9cc407d58f0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJxKg\"}"}